    "created_at": "2019-11-30T17:50:06Z",
    "updated_at": "2019-11-30T17:58:04Z",
    "body": "A simple fix seems to be to replace the PROMPT_COMMAND line in the [starship.bash](https://github.com/starship/starship/blob/82cfb6bdb9881bbdc9a535555abae1ce8eba724e/src/init/starship.bash#L64) file with:\r\n\r\n```bash\r\nPROMPT_COMMAND=\"$PROMPT_COMMAND;starship_precmd;\"\r\n```\r\n\r\nI am not really sure as to why this fixed it though. If someone knows why this is the case, an explanation would be appreciated.\r\n\r\nEDIT:\r\nIf you want to fix this locally, you can clear the prompt command before evaluating starship. Although make sure that you are not using the prompt command for anything else that you might need.\r\n\r\n```bash\r\nexport PROMPT_COMMAND=\"\"\r\neval \"$(starship init bash)\"\r\n```",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
